course: dictionary
lesson: 5835
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have lots of meanings. The word major is one of them. To find the right meaning, read the sentence and ask which meaning fits. «Billie Eilish and her brother recorded her album at home, and it won major awards.» Here major means very important or very big, because the awards are a big deal.
explain: Major can also be a rank in the army, a kind of musical key that sounds bright and happy, or a student's main subject at university. You can tell which one by the words around it. Music words like key or scale point to music. Words like studied or university point to school.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. «In the UK food businesses must tell people which of 14 major allergens are in their food.» Swap in very important: the allergens are the important ones to name, so it fits. If your meaning does not fit, try another meaning from the list.
fact: Major is an adjective when it means big, serious or important, as in «a major road».
fact: «Major» can mean very important, very big or very serious.
fact: In music, a major key sounds bright and happy, as in C major.
fact: In the army, a major is an officer of middle rank.
fact: In the US and Canada, your major is the main subject you study at university, and «she majored in maths» means maths was her main subject.
exercise: In the UK food businesses must tell people which of 14 major allergens are in their food. What does major mean here? | *Very important or big | An army officer | A school subject | A bright, happy tune
exercise: Sam says C major is a key in music. What does major mean in music? | A very sad sound | A kind of star | *A bright, happy sound | A loud drum beat
exercise: «She majored in maths at university.» What does majored mean? | Failed the maths test | *Studied it as her main subject | Forgot all her maths | Taught maths to small children
test: «Billie Eilish's debut album won major awards.» Which word means about the same as major here? | Wet and grey | Tiny and quiet | *Big and important | Old and broken
test: In the army, what is a major? | A type of food | *An officer of middle rank | A kind of star | A long, straight road
exam: «Hangry is now in major dictionaries.» Which meaning fits best here? | Studying as a main subject at university | *Big and important | A bright, happy key in music | An army rank
